The current text carries much of the standard, but three places can steer the model to drop evidence the standard keeps: the carmaker example, retold quarterly guidance, and the treatment of existing arrangements. The carmaker example, for instance, labels a market-share figure as noise even though it gives no basis for deciding whether that figure matters to the parts supplier being studied.

This audit judges [review-core-t2.txt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/review-core-t2.txt) against [the version 4 standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html). I do **not** count the loss of §6’s optional items as a breach. “No source” means I could not find the instruction itself on the standard page; it does not by itself prove the instruction will cause a wrong drop.

### Opening

1. **“Before you return the answer, check it once.”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “从第一段读到最后一段，分析员会记的都留。一页有八条就是八条，不挑”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** A final check does not itself change the keep rule, although checking an existing list cannot recover evidence that was never added to it.

2. **“Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “一个在追这家公司的分析员，读到会在本周笔记里写下来，因为它让某个问题的答案更可能或更不可能。”  
   **CONSISTENT.** This carries the analyst’s keep test.

3. **“about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “问题不限于库里已有的，也不限于本公司：客户、供应商、竞争者、监管、宏观都算”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** The named scope follows the standard, though the standard’s four kinds also explicitly name partners.

4. **“Ask first whether it is new”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “判一句话之前先问：这是新信息吗？”; §5.3: “看不出是旧事的不算重提”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** Asking first follows the standard, but the text does not carry the instruction not to call something a retelling when the words and date do not establish that.

5. **“repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “重复常识、描述长期状况、泛泛的看法，是杂音”; “不是常识的，是新信息……分析员会记就留”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** These are the standard’s noise classes, provided a new, relevant statement about an old situation is still judged as new information.

6. **“guidance, a forecast or a plan still in force keeps its place even when retold”**  
   Standard, §5.3: “重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量”.  
   **WIDER-DROP.** The text can be read as requiring retold guidance to be still in force, whereas the standard separately protects retold quarterly guidance and applies “仍然有效” to forecasts and plans.

7. **“These usually fail that check:”**  
   Standard, §5.2: “下面的不留清单不能用来删掉分析员会记的陈述”; §6: “先看那一行的‘边界’一列”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** “Usually” leaves room for the analyst test, but the individual examples must still carry their boundaries.

### Background and common knowledge

8. **“background the analyst already knew”**  
   Standard, §5.1: “常识，就是跟这家公司的分析员读这篇之前就已经知道的”.  
   **CONSISTENT.** The condition follows the standard’s definition of common knowledge.

9. **“an arrangement already in place, described again”**  
   Standard, §5.3: “重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量”; §5.2: “下面的不留清单不能用来删掉分析员会记的陈述”.  
   **WIDER-DROP.** An arrangement already in place can describe a still-effective plan or carry a relevant fact, and its existence alone does not establish that the standard rejects it.

10. **“a long-standing situation retold, with no new figure or claim about it”**  
    Standard, §5.1: “描述长期状况……是杂音”; “不是常识的，是新信息……分析员会记就留”.  
    **CONSISTENT.** The qualification excludes a new figure or claim, so a genuinely unchanged retelling follows the noise rule.

