18. **“if demand slows it would hurt”**  
    Standard, §5.3: “如果 AI 退潮会受伤”; §5.2: “不因为……‘离现在远’……就不留”.  
    **CONSISTENT.** This is analogous to the standard’s unsupported general-risk example; being conditional alone remains insufficient to reject evidence.

19. **“a figure alone does not lift it”**  
    Standard, §5.1: “有数字也要过上面的规则”.  
    **CONSISTENT.** A number alone does not replace the analyst’s relevance judgment.

20. **“the leading carmaker has held a third of its home market for a decade”, in an article about a parts supplier**  
    Standard, §5.1: “作者说‘英特尔多年领先，占 CPU 市场 59%’，和英伟达的问题关系不大，分析员不会记”.  
    **EXAMPLE-DISAGREES.** The standard rejects its example because it has little connection to the company’s questions; the new example supplies no such reason, and a leading carmaker’s market share could matter to a parts supplier.

